  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Comes a Time** (2 reviews): Comes a Time leads into a Lost Sailor jam, and Garcia comments on it; the band had done this three other times; Garcia remarks that Comes a Time flows straight into Sailor>Circumstance, and the band can be heard grooving toward it [3][4]\n- **Tons of Steel** (1 review): The false start on Tons of Steel exposes an unexplored darker side of the tune [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Tons of Steel - false start # 1**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Tons of Steel - false start # 2**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Comes a Time**: back after 348 archived shows (1662 days) [5]\n- **Mississippi Half Step - false start**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Green Onions**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **Uncle John's Band - false start**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Beam & Percussion//**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1985-04-21.121757.sbd.Lestatkatt.flac16** (recommended): soundboard; 17 songs; 92 min [1]\n- **gd1985-04-21.sbd.seaweed.121733.flac1644**: soundboard; 16 songs; 92 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [2]. Said about its sound: The mix is somewhat muffled [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- This transfer is better quality than the other, whose tape garbling during Uncle John's Band makes listening unpleasant [3]\n- Reviewer heard many soulful Comes a Time versions in 1985, usually in the night's final ballad slot [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1985-04-21.121757.sbd.Lestatkatt.flac16**: transferred by Lestatkatt; source: Source: SBD > ?>Low Gen Maxell XLII Cassette>Wav>Soundforge 10 (Tracking, Pitch Correction and *Editing)>Flac [1]. Also: Transfer from an old cassette labeled Practice Sessions, March 1985, owned since the late 1980s; no noise reduction used; Side one ended with Green Onions and 20 seconds of Uncle John's Band; side two fades in mid-intro, so uploader edited them together [1]\n- **gd1985-04-21.sbd.seaweed.121733.flac1644**: taped by seaweed1010; transferred by Andrew F.; source: Source: SBD > ? > Cassette, kindly provided by Seaweed1010. [2]. Also: Tape is labeled 4/21 but may be a compilation of tracks from different days; songs don't match Deadbase listing [2]",
